prompt_template:
Create one finished {ASPECT_RATIO} experimental fashion editorial poster, edge-to-edge canvas, no mockup. A cold human-machine body study on pure white. Prioritized style rules: {STYLE_FIDELITY_ANCHORS}
Subject: {SUBJECT}
Design and ratio adaptation: {DESIGN_DIRECTION}
Exact compact headline: "{MAIN_TEXT}". Exact small supporting line: "{SECONDARY_TEXT}". Exact small identifier: "{CATALOG_CODE}". Print each once, no other lettering, numerals or brands. Typography is perfectly solid orange, clean and smaller than the dominant figure: a technical editorial margin, NOT a giant advertising headline. It may rotate 90 degrees as a readable complete line. Keep all letters unoccluded and inside the canvas with visible white separation from the figure. At most a few tiny orange registration marks.
Rendering: painterly realism and editorial collage, NOT a pristine photo. Use broad scraped enamel marks, large angular brush planes in clothing, selectively unfinished figure edges and strong black masses. Orange hardware has gray metal and muted olive paint beneath chips; face and anatomy convincing with painterly simplification. White paper has no texture. Sculptural light, no scene or horizon.
Replace source content: {SOURCE_CONTENT_TO_AVOID}. No ecology metaphors, flowers, animals, gardening, apples, copied shoulder armor, action combat, weapons, city backgrounds, neon, CGI gloss, corporate ads, motivational slogans, logos or watermarks.
